{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8d4640ef4d158be0a6db3a7228998a3d82993e21701395b55e21bda0e0e0b5cf","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"samholt/l2mac@105e74afdc67 snapshot 3bdf23d1d7da66dc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5da6ca2c5a7c67261046709126c8cbfefc2c38283010a89786f27d15a9eb2df0","slc_c133f07c4fc04ce8647c0211a5c4d246564aa571f9efdccb4203967a4b7e0313","slc_e42ae7ac665ade7d05545f21e9bad043de03987413b8d886b133ec89e700fcba","slc_fe1b66b18b7fdf04f26e02bdd40035d5d2e85abadbd8af3b9486530a2ff517fc"],"source_ids":["src_49df1e30bf5757a4a3b97f525fdd4e75"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors join the dev team by submitting a PR, with ongoing tasks listed on the roadmap; a rotating Chief Evangelist community role is recruited via email.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9898baa4293b785f998b047fd9e75ac557663249290b5c00743af2b494cdeb29","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"samholt/l2mac@105e74afdc67 snapshot 3bdf23d1d7da66dc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_449ed80cc86a3dd6a1dbb8d193dc86ebc5e8d6e659feddca47b017f53e024914"],"source_ids":["src_bf415efb5e1055d583ada98510945b8a"],"text":"The prompt-program is a sequence of instruction-step prompts; unless explicitly given, it is self-generated (bootstrapped) and then executed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a04e8c4b1684de0695edef34e3e9c971362ac1e985cbd39229659a81c88738c6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"samholt/l2mac@105e74afdc67 snapshot 3bdf23d1d7da66dc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4258f7b1fe2630d24e84596381b53ed3737e4dcdc737d0b14e5437e75adf4bdb","slc_e9bdf2c0e968584d201260a89e83bad7ccc6b33e0fb49c91230b87ec8a560df4"],"source_ids":["src_bf415efb5e1055d583ada98510945b8a"],"text":"L2MAC is described as an LLM-based multi-agent system implementing a stored-program von Neumann-style architecture for extensive, consistent output generation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a3587c5c5ca174845d6e4cafea96026f314e4869f60627c583f8ac65ba34533d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"samholt/l2mac@105e74afdc67 snapshot 3bdf23d1d7da66dc","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_266a95c55e6bd0e5c06f98b4c6221eabecf3acb3552da522b9dc66831a3e6ec0","slc_2e37795a34d5bac40bf9be3df7cfc248b51bac1e496ba5e51fab1dc272c6d77f","slc_45546ddb937652c3a9285be0a8b2d01872525e428ca86ba8d750970990a8ff8d","slc_5c930c5e61eee2955426c1521297e9cd1a56516efd52f549d1379ce5bf448a50","slc_b68dc64d99980151e4764e791a69692f8e6b8c73b89976ad301bd424ca90b2e6","slc_bb27407357215d55bd7b336d15793edbf931c90ac40b5fa04570c3f3f03896c8"],"source_ids":["src_4a6a47553b785f45bfc693b1bed74c49","src_bf415efb5e1055d583ada98510945b8a"],"text":"L2MAC offers a CLI (e.g. `l2mac \"...\"` creating a codebase repo in ./workspace) and a Python library API including generate_codebase and run_l2mac, plus helper functions for book and custom domains.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:39:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_528de8705e784752be8205edc0189def"}
